<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Triumvirate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Triumvirate was the political alliance formed in 43 BCE by Octavian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Lepidus to rule the Roman state after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. It defeated Caesar's assassins and carried out proscriptions of its opponents. Its breakdown led to the war between Octavian and Antony, from which Octavian emerged as Augustus, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate.jpg" alt="Second Triumvirate" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: You may select the license of your choice. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antony_with_Octavian_aureus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
